                 ENDF/B-VII.1.beta EVALUATION                     9440 1451     
                                                                  9440 1451     
  P.G.Young, P.Talou, M.B.Chadwick, A. C. Kahler, and T. Kawano   9440 1451     
                (LANL, 24 September 2009)                         9440 1451     
                          and                                     9440 1451     
               H.Derrien, L.C.Leal, D.Wiarda                      9440 1451     
                   (ORNL, July 2010)                              9440 1451     
                                                                  9440 1451     
                    ----- SUMMARY -----                           9440 1451     
                                                                  9440 1451     
Major features of the ENDF/B-VII.1 evaluation are:                9440 1451     
                                                                  9440 1451     
1. New covariance evaluations of nubar and the total, (n,gamma),  9440 1451     
and (n,f) cross sections that utilize ENDF/B-VII standards data   9440 1451     
are incorporated. All available experimental data was included in 9440 1451     
each covariance analysis, using the GLUCS code by Hetrick and Fu  9440 1451     
(He80).  The output included most probable cross sections or      9440 1451     
multiplicities, standard deviations, and correlations.            9440 1451     
                                                                  9440 1451     
2. A new ORNL evaluation (July 2010) was performed, extending the 9440 1451     
resolved resonance range up to 5.7 keV.                           9440 1451     
                                                                  9440 1451     
3. A new prompt fission neutron spectrum evaluation was performed 9440 1451     
using the Los Alamos model, as well as an uncertainty             9440 1451     
quantification study for the 0.5 MeV neutron-induced spectrum.    9440 1451     
                                                                  9440 1451     
4. New reaction theory calculations are utilized for (n,xn) and   9440 1451     
other reactions.  Direct reaction cross sections and angular      9440 1451     
distributions are extended to an excitation energy of 4 MeV based 9440 1451     
on the 238U ENDF/B-VII evaluation.                                9440 1451     
                                                                  9440 1451     
5. Fission product yields, delayed-neutron data, and photon-      9440 1451     
production data are carried over from ENDF/B-VII.                 9440 1451     
                                                                  9440 1451     
6. Uncertainty quantification of all major reaction cross-sections9440 1451     
(MF=33, MT=1,2,4,16,17,18,102) and of the prompt fission neutron  9440 1451     
spectrum (MF=35, MT=18) and prompt fission neutron multiplicity   9440 1451     
(MF=31, MT=456).                                                  9440 1451     
                                                                  9440 1451     
             ----- DETAILED DESCRIPTION -----                     9440 1451     
                                                                  9440 1451     
>> MF=1 GENERAL INFORMATION                                       9440 1451     
                                                                  9440 1451     
MT=452: Total Average Neutron Multiplicity per Fission (Total     9440 1451     
        Nubar)                                                    9440 1451     
   Sum of MT=455 and 456.                                         9440 1451     
                                                                  9440 1451     
MT=455: Average Delayed Neutron Multiplicity per Fission          9440 1451     
   The ENDF/B-VII evaluation was adopted.                         9440 1451     
                                                                  9440 1451     
MT=456: Average Prompt Neutron Multiplicity per Fission           9440 1451     
   The JENDL actinoid evaluation (Iw08), multiplied by a factor of9440 1451     
1.00122 to bring correspondance with ENDF/B-VII standards, was    9440 1451     
adopted.  We verified the evaluation by performing a covariance   9440 1451     
analysis of the experimental database between 100 keV and 15 MeV, 9440 1451     
using the GLUCS code by Hetrick and Fu (He80)  Above 15 MeV, we   9440 1451     
linearly extrapolated the data below 15 MeV to 30 MeV.            9440 1451     
                                                                  9440 1451     
MT=458:  Energy Release from Fission                              9440 1451     
   The ENDF/B-VII evaluation, which is based on the analysis by   9440 1451     
Sher (Sh83), was adopted.                                         9440 1451     
