----- UNRESOLVED RESONANCE PARAMETERS (5.7 - 40 keV) -----        9440 1451     
                                                                  9440 1451     
>> MF=3 NEUTRON CROSS SECTIONS                                    9440 1451     
                                                                  9440 1451     
              ----- GENERAL INFORMATION -----                     9440 1451     
                                                                  9440 1451     
   The total (MT=1), fission (MT=18), and radiative capture       9440 1451     
(MT=102) cross sections are based mainly on experimental data,    9440 1451     
complimented by nuclear model calculations. The experimental data 9440 1451     
were analyzed with the covariance code GLUCS (He80).  Model       9440 1451     
parameters for the calculations were obtained by optimization with9440 1451     
the experimental data.                                            9440 1451     
   The ECIS94 coupled-channels optical model code (Ra94) was used 9440 1451     
with a slightly modified version of the Sukovitskii optical model 9440 1451     
potential (Su04) for all discrete (n,n) and (n,n') cross section  9440 1451     
and angular distribution calculations, as well as for calculating 9440 1451     
neutron transmission coefficients for the reaction theory         9440 1451     
calculations. The modification we made to the Sukovitskii         9440 1451     
potential consisted of decreasing the lambda parameter in the     9440 1451     
imaginary surface derivative potential, Wd, from 0.01759 to 0.010.9440 1451     
   Reaction theory calculations, utilizing the GNASH (Yo98) and   9440 1451     
COMNUC (Du70) Hauser-Feshbach codes, were used for (n,xn)         9440 1451     
reactions, again with the model parameters optimized to           9440 1451     
experimental data. The GNASH calculations also include            9440 1451     
preequilibrium contributions.                                     9440 1451     
                                                                  9440 1451     
           ----- DETAILS OF MF = 3 DATA -----                     9440 1451     
                                                                  9440 1451     
MT=1: Total Cross Section                                         9440 1451     
                                                                  9440 1451     
0  - 40 keV                                                       9440 1451     
  Data were obtained from the JENDL actinoid evaluation, but were 9440 1451     
renormalized slightly to match the covariance analysis above 40   9440 1451     
keV. The shape of the cross sections below 40 keV follows the     9440 1451     
Sukovitskii optical model calculation closely.                    9440 1451     
                                                                  9440 1451     
40 keV - 30 MeV                                                   9440 1451     
  The evaluation of the neutron total cross section in the MeV    9440 1451     
region resulted from a covariance analysis with the GLUCS code    9440 1451     
(He80) of the experimental data. Experimental data used were those9440 1451     
of Po81, Po83, and Sm72. We used the optical model results from   9440 1451     
Sukovitskii (Su04) as the prior in the GLUCS analysis, and the    9440 1451     
analysis results are very close to the optical model values at all9440 1451     
energies.  The evaluated total cross section is a smooth curve    9440 1451     
through the covariance analysis results, and above 8 MeV is       9440 1451     
identically equal to the optical model calculation.               9440 1451     
                                                                  9440 1451     
MT=2: Elastic Scattering Cross Section                            9440 1451     
                                                                  9440 1451     
   The elastic cross section is obtained by subtracting the       9440 1451     
nonelastic cross section (MT=3) from the total cross section      9440 1451     
(MT=1).  It is consistent with Sukovitskii's (Su04) optical       9440 1451     
results.                                                          9440 1451     
                                                                  9440 1451     
MT=3: Nonelastic Cross Section                                    9440 1451     
                                                                  9440 1451     
   The (redundant) nonelastic cross section is the sum of         9440 1451     
MT=4,16,17,18,37,102.                                             9440 1451     
                                                                  9440 1451     
MT=4: Inelastic Cross Section                                     9440 1451     
                                                                  9440 1451     
   Sum of MT=51-91.                                               9440 1451     
                                                                  9440 1451     
MT=16,17,37: (n,xn) Cross Sections                                9440 1451     
                                                                  9440 1451     
   The (n,xn) cross sections (and energy-angle distributions)     9440 1451     
result from our GNASH (Yo98) calculations. The (n,2n) cross       9440 1451     
section is somewhat higher near 14 MeV than the earlier ENDF/B-   9440 1451     
VII, JEFF-3.1, and JENDL-3.3 evaluations but is lower than the    9440 1451     
recent JENDL actinoid (Iw08) evaluation.                          9440 1451     
                                                                  9440 1451     
MT=18: Fission Neutron Cross Section                              9440 1451     
                                                                  9440 1451     
0 - 550 keV                                                       9440 1451     
   The cross section at these energies was taken from the JENDL   9440 1451     
actinoid evaluation.  These data agree well with the results of a 9440 1451     
GLUCS covariance analysis of the experimental data from 60 keV -  9440 1451     
30 MeV, where they overlap.                                       9440 1451     
                                                                  9440 1451     
550 keV - 30 MeV                                                  9440 1451     
   The (n,f) cross section in this energy range is based on a     9440 1451     
smooth curve through the GLUCS covariance analysis results. These 9440 1451     
results are influenced strongly by the extensive measurements of  9440 1451     
Staples et al. (St98).  At some energies in this range, the       9440 1451     
present evaluation differs appreciably from the ENDF/B-VII, JEFF- 9440 1451     
3.1, JENDL-3.3, AND JENDL actinoid evaluations.  The GNASH        9440 1451     
analysis closely follows the evaluation at most energies.         9440 1451     
                                                                  9440 1451     
MT=19,20,21,38: Multi-Chance Fission Cross Sections               9440 1451     
                                                                  9440 1451     
  The multichance fission cross sections are obtained by scaling  9440 1451     
the GNASH calculations of the MT=19,20,21,38 cross sections by the9440 1451     
ratio of the new evaluated MT=18 cross section to the GNASH total 9440 1451     
fission cross section.                                            9440 1451     
                                                                  9440 1451     
MT=51-90 Discrete Inelastic Level Cross Sections                  9440 1451     
                                                                  9440 1451     
     Mt=51-54: Ground-state rotational band direct and compound   9440 1451     
nucleus cross sections taken from ECIS96 calculations with our    9440 1451     
modified version of the Sukovitskii optical model potential       9440 1451     
(Su04).                                                           9440 1451     
     MT=55-71: Compound nucleus cross sections taken from ECIS96  9440 1451     
calculations with our modified version of the Sukovitskii optical 9440 1451     
model potential (Su04).                                           9440 1451     
     MT=72-90: Cross sections for grouped collective 2+ and 3-    9440 1451     
states are assumed to be the same as for 238U(n,n') reactions and 9440 1451     
were taken for the ENDF/B-VII 238U evaluation.  Those data, in    9440 1451     
turn, are based on DWBA/vibrational model calculations performed  9440 1451     
with the ECIS94 code (Ra94), assuming a set of 2+ or 3-           9440 1451     
vibrational states.  Deformation parameters were determined by    9440 1451     
matching the 14-MeV Baba measurements (Ba89) of neutron emission  9440 1451     
spectra at various angles.  The calculations were used to         9440 1451     
extrapolate the 14-MeV cross sections to lower and higher         9440 1451     
energies, and to obtain the MF=4 angular distributions for each   9440 1451     
assumed state. The spins, parities, and deformation parameters    9440 1451     
used in the calculations are given in the table below. These      9440 1451     
results affect the evaluation in the excitation energy range      9440 1451     
Ex=1.17-3.91 MeV.                                                 9440 1451     
